)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Status Panel -- Action Characters        !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                  }
}  Type an action character in the NP column of a job and press Enter.
}  You can type them on several lines at once.
}
{   ?  }Show the job's data sets (Job Data Set panel).
{   S  }Browse the job's output (Output Data Set panel).
{   D  }Display the job: JES2 answers with its status ($D).
{   L  }List the job's output: JES2 answers with its data sets ($L).
{   C  }Cancel the job ($C). Its output stays.
{   CD }Cancel the job with a dump ($C with D).
{   P  }Purge the job: cancel it and delete its output. The list is read
}       again at once.
{   A  }Release a held job ($A).
{   H  }Hold the job ($H). A held job waiting to execute does not start.
{   E  }Restart the job ($E): JES2 puts it back on the input queue.
{   O  }Release the job's held output for printing ($O).
}
}  JES2's answers go to the system log (LOG); the panel says COMMAND
}  ISSUED. D and L need read access to the job, the others update access;
}  your own jobs you may always act on. Without the access the panel says
}  NOT AUTHORIZED FOR JOB.
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: Status panel help   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHSTF
  &ZUP = ISFHST
)END
